## Evidence gap

The legacy `events.csv` row `zaf-murp-afdb-approved-2026` records a USD 400
million AfDB approval for Mpumalanga municipal utility reform, dated
2026-07-16. Its `source_id` is `zaf-murp-afdb-2026`, but the legacy row has
no `document_sha256` and only the broad locator “official announcement.”
Ticket [[0926]] subsequently collected the publisher HTML: retrieval
`zaf-murp-afdb-2026:2` at `data/jetp/retrievals.csv:321` is HTTP 200 via
`browser-session`, with SHA-256
`a9385e879af5f88511324674b8b12345cea23bc3dd0fbc8eae3b02a11e57cf33`.
The corresponding `manifest.csv:321` entry names
`objects/a9/a9385e879af5f88511324674b8b12345cea23bc3dd0fbc8eae3b02a11e57cf33.html`.
Collection closed the snapshot gap; it did not supply a cited line or a
reviewed agreement identity. The 0876 pending register therefore reports
`missing_precise_cited_line`, and the event must not become an observation
from the headline alone.

## Work

- Materialize the archived HTML with `make jetp-data`; inspect its rendered
  article body and identify the exact approval statement, date, amount,
  instrument, borrower/beneficiary, and any distinction between loan approval,
  signature, and disbursement.
- Add a ledger line with the archived SHA and a precise paragraph or heading
  locator. Adjudicate the subject as a distinct agreement, an existing
  agreement, or a source-row-only referent, documenting the identity basis.
- Add the event-specific decision for 0876 and regenerate its pending and
  reconciliation outputs. Preserve the legacy source view bytes and leave
  unsupported financial stages pending.

## Exit criteria

- [x] The archived publisher statement, exact locator, snapshot hash, and
  financial stage are recorded in a cited ledger line.
- [x] The event has one reviewed subject decision with a line-referent, or
  an explicit documented reason to keep it pending.
- [x] The 0876 register and all 451 legacy timing rows reconcile after
  rebuild; no approval is promoted to signature or disbursement.
- [x] `make jetp-ledger-check`, focused source/reconciliation tests,
  `make check-fast`, and `make lint` run; any full-gate obstacle is recorded
  by test or preflight ID.

## Verification (commit a20034c2)

- `data/jetp/lines.d/ZAF-2026.csv:308` records the archived SHA-256,
  article `#node-95536` body paragraph 1, and `approved` money stage.
  The archived HTML byte hash was verified locally after `make jetp-data`
  could not sync `pytest==9.0.2` in the network-restricted worktree; the
  complete pinned 275-object DVC document set was reflink-copied from an
  existing worktree with the same `documents.dvc` pointer.
- `data/jetp/line-referents.csv:383` and
  `data/jetp/migration/1120-event-adjudications.csv:2` review the distinct
  MURP loan agreement. `data/jetp/observations.csv:259` accepts only the
  USD 400 million approval. `data/jetp/migration/0876-pending.csv:2` holds
  the unsupported 16 July event-day timing. The publisher page labels that
  date as publication; the separate AfDB catalogue gives 15 July approval,
  but its line has not yet been archived in the ledger.
- `tests/test_jetp_1120_murp.py::test_1120_source_identity_stage_and_date_are_separate`
  checks source digest, referent, amount, status and held timing.
  `tests/test_jetp_observations.py::test_current_ledger_accounts_for_every_event_without_inventing_a_citation`
  checks 448 accepted observations plus three held events and all 451
  legacy timing rows. Two consecutive rebuilds produced identical hashes;
  all four served legacy observation JSON files remained byte identical.
- `make jetp-ledger-check` passed; focused replay checks passed (14 tests);
  `make check-fast` passed with local socket access (2,370 passed, 13 skipped);
  `make lint` passed (338 passed, 12 skipped). Independent reviewer found no
  substantive issue. `make check` stopped at
  `scripts/qa_full_gate_preflight.py`: missing bulk corpus, reranker cache
  (ticket [[0592]]), and 80 JETP CRS inputs, plus local socket and Git
  worktree administration restrictions in the sandbox.
